    "objectID": "usage.html#what-is-currently-not-supported",
    "href": "usage.html#what-is-currently-not-supported",
    "title": "How to use MAMMA MIA",
    "section": "What is currently not supported",
    "text": "What is currently not supported\nObservation based input datasets for a trajectory, where time is an observation and not a dimension. e.g. PARCELS output datasets.\nSurface simulated payloads, MAMMA MIA currently only supports using 3D datasets, and can only interpolate within the model/dataset boundaries. Since most 3D parameters in models have an shallowest depth of around 0.5 metres this means there is no payload simulated when the glider or other platforms are on the surface.\nThe planned solution for this is to switch to a suitable surface field parameter when the platform is at the surface (since most models will have one), which also means MAMMA MIA will be able to support airborne platforms observing the ocean surface.",
