    "objectID": "simulators.html#slocum-gliders",
    "href": "simulators.html#slocum-gliders",
    "title": "Simulators",
    "section": "Slocum Gliders",
    "text": "Slocum Gliders\nMAMMA MIA provides a simplified interface with glidersim, it also provides an integration with glidersim providing environmental data like u/v currents and temperature and salinity when it is running a mission simulation.\n\nMission builder\nMAMMA MIA provides an GliderMissionBuilder class that allows users to create Slocum glider missions without having to configure glidersim directly.\nThere are two missions that can be built (more will be added), a virtual_mooring and follow_waypoints.\n\nVirtual Mooring\nThe code snippet below shows how to configure and run a virtual mooring mission.\nfrom mamma_mia import GliderMissionBuilder\n\nvirtual_mooring = GliderMissionBuilder.virtual_mooring(\n    mission_name=\"rapid-mooring_spiral\",\n    datetime_str=\"2023-03-03T12:00:00:Z\",\n    description=\"RAPID ARRAY spiral simulation\",\n    glider_model=\"DEEP\",\n    inital_heading=225,\n    lat_ini=27.225,\n    lon_ini=-15.4225,\n    glider_name=\"comet\",\n    mission_directory=\"RAPID-mooring_spiral\",\n    dive_depth=1000,\n    spiral=False\n)\n\nvirtual_mooring.run_mission(maxSimulationTime=2,verbose=True) # 2 days\nvirtual_mooring.save_mission()\nThis snippet creates a virtual mooring mission, starting at midnight on the 3rd March 2023 at 27.225 degrees N and -15.4225 degrees E, diving to 1000 metres.\nThen the mission is ran for 2 days and finally saved (important for MAMMA MIA to import the trajectory).\nThe output will be a NetCDF file that can be specified as input to a MAMMAMIA mission.\n\n\nFollow Waypoints\nThe second mission type that can be created is follow_waypoints:\nfrom mamma_mia import GliderMissionBuilder\n\nwaypoints = GliderMissionBuilder.follow_waypoints(\n    mission_name=\"waypoints2\",\n    datetime_str=\"2023-03-03T12:00:00:Z\",\n    description=\"follow waypoints simulation\",\n    glider_model=\"DEEP\",\n    inital_heading=225,\n    lat_ini=27.225,\n    lon_ini=-15.4225,\n    lat_wp=[27.425,27.825,28.205,28.503],\n    lon_wp=[-15.4225,-15.4225,-15.4225,-15.4225],\n    glider_name=\"comet\",\n    mission_directory=\"waypoints2\",\n    dive_depth=1000\n)\n\nwaypoints.run_mission(maxSimulationTime=7,verbose=True) # 7 days\nwaypoints.save_mission()\nThis snippet will start at 27.225 degrees N, -15.4225 degrees East and will try and head to the next way point as specified in the lat_wp and lon_wp lists. While doing this will be diving to 1000 metres. Once it reaches the first way point it will then head to the second.\nThe mission is then run for 7 days, NOTE the glider may not reach all waypoints as that will depend on its ability to travel to them in the time simulated.\nFinally the mission is exported and can again be used as input into MAMMAMIA",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Simulators"
    ]
  },
