  {
    "objectID": "structure.html#mamma-mia-structure",
    "href": "structure.html#mamma-mia-structure",
    "title": "Structure",
    "section": "",
    "text": "MAMMA MIA output contains the following hierarchical structure:\n\nCampaign: contains one or more missions\n\nMissions: contains a single platform deployment with one or more sensors\n\npayload: contains the simulated sensor payload for the deployment",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Structure"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "structure.html#campaigns",
    "href": "structure.html#campaigns",
    "title": "MAMMA MIA structure",
    "section": "Campaigns",
    "text": "Campaigns\nCampaigns contain all the missions for a given set of deployments. They can contain one or more missions each with its self contained set of meta data, world data and simulated payload.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Structure"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "structure.html#missions",
    "href": "structure.html#missions",
    "title": "MAMMA MIA structure",
    "section": "Missions",
    "text": "Missions\nThis is a single platform deployment, it contains multiple sections:\n\nPayload: simulated data\nPlatform: metadata for platform\nWorlds: gridded model data that has been used to simulate observations",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Structure"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "structure.html#payload",
    "href": "structure.html#payload",
    "title": "MAMMA MIA structure",
    "section": "Payload",
    "text": "Payload\nThis contains all the simulated data ranging from:\n\ndatalogger: contains flight information like position, pitch, yaw etc\nCTD: simulated temperature, pressure and salinity",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Structure"
=======
    "objectID": "future_dev.html",
    "href": "future_dev.html",
    "title": "Future Development",
    "section": "",
    "text": "This page details the future development plans for the MAMMA MIA python module.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Future Development"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "future_dev.html#support-for-airborne-platforms",
    "href": "future_dev.html#support-for-airborne-platforms",
    "title": "Future Development",
    "section": "Support for Airborne Platforms",
    "text": "Support for Airborne Platforms\nCurrently only subsurface platforms are supported, MAMMA MIA also does not simulate payloads at the surface (approx less than 0.5 m) due to needing to switch to a different data product at this point (from a 3D to a surface field). Future work will make this seamless and also introduce the option of simulating the payloads of airborne platforms, and introducing new observation types such as swaths.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Future Development"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "future_dev.html#support-for-lagrangian-drifters-e.g.-argo-floats",
    "href": "future_dev.html#support-for-lagrangian-drifters-e.g.-argo-floats",
    "title": "Future Development",
    "section": "Support for Lagrangian Drifters (e.g. ARGO floats)",
    "text": "Support for Lagrangian Drifters (e.g. ARGO floats)\nMAMMA MIA currently doesn’t support a typical Lagrangian python library output (PARCELS), this is due to the fact that PARCELS output does not have a time dimension but is an effectively a 2D array of observations and drifters. This support will be implemented so an ARGO simulator can be integrated into MAMMA MIA.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Future Development"
    ]
  },
  {
