    "section": "Support for Lagrangian Drifters (e.g. ARGO floats)",
    "text": "Support for Lagrangian Drifters (e.g. ARGO floats)\nMAMMA MIA currently doesn’t support a typical Lagrangian python library output (PARCELS), this is due to the fact that PARCELS output does not have a time dimension but is an effectively a 2D array of observations and drifters. This support will be implemented so an ARGO simulator can be integrated into MAMMA MIA.",
